Tutorial 5 — Sharing a Credential and Revoking Access.
Planning timestamps generated from the script's scene budgets.
Re-time against the final edit before publishing (see docs/video-tutorials.md).

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:07.400
You control who sees your credentials.

2
00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:14.400
Share links give a specific verifier time-
limited access, and you can revoke

3
00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:20.110
them at any time.

4
00:00:45.500 --> 00:00:52.400
Create a link for your credential.

5
00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:59.400
Set how many hours it lasts, between one
and eight thousand seven hundred sixty,

6
00:00:59.500 --> 00:01:06.400
and choose view only or download.

7
00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:13.400
Adding a password is optional but
recommended.

8
00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:20.400
The response contains a token; send it to
the verifier through a private

9
00:01:20.500 --> 00:01:23.008
channel.

10
00:02:15.500 --> 00:02:22.400
The verifier validates the token, with the
password if you set one.

11
00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:29.400
They get the credential ID, the
permission, and when the link expires.

12
00:02:29.500 --> 00:02:36.400
After it expires the link stops working.

13
00:03:30.500 --> 00:03:37.400
Changed your mind?

14
00:03:37.500 --> 00:03:44.400
Delete the share link.

15
00:03:44.500 --> 00:03:51.400
Any later attempt to validate it fails
straight away.

16
00:04:30.500 --> 00:04:37.400
Share for the shortest time that works,
use a password, and revoke links you no

17
00:04:37.500 --> 00:04:39.868
longer need.

18
00:04:39.968 --> 00:04:46.038
That's the end of this series.

19
00:04:46.138 --> 00:04:50.152
Thanks for watching.
